<title>BELGIUM: Belgian OLO auction raises further 7.185 bln bfr.</title>
<headline>Belgian OLO auction raises further 7.185 bln bfr.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian Treasury gave the following details about the outcome of its monthly auction -</p>
<p>BELA</p>
<p>* 6.25 pct, March 28, 2007</p>
<p>    Avg weighted price / yield   104.507 / 5.650 pct</p>
<p>    Price range of bids	    104.40 to 104.55</p>
<p>    Stop (lowest accepted) price 104.50</p>
<p>    Allotted at non-comp auction   6.450 billion francs (*)</p>
<p>    Allotted at comp auction	10.025 billion francs</p>
<p>* 8.75 pct, June 25, 2002 OLO</p>
<p>    Avg weighted price / yield   118.950 / 4.644 pct</p>
<p>    Price range of bids	    118.80/95</p>
<p>    Stop (lowest accepted) price 118.95</p>
<p>    Allotted at non-comp auction   0.735 billion (*)</p>
<p>    Allotted at comp auction	 3.800 billion</p>
<p>NOTE: Total sales at competitive and non-competitive (*)</p>
<p>auction 21.010 bln bfr</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
